{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/334233-genesis-engines-and-dragonlords-fluff-dragonblooded","id":334233,"title":"Genesis Engines and Dragonlords [Fluff] [Dragonblooded]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-08T08:57:48-08:00","id":334233,"title":"Genesis Engines and Dragonlords [Fluff] [Dragonblooded]","content":"The Engines Of Genesis are cousins to the Shards Of Divinity, tens of thousands made between the Elemental Dragons in a frenzy of fecund creation. Imbued in a hand-picked number of human men and nine times that many women to start a fecund frenzy anew. Each bearer was a Terrestrial Exalt of legendary breeding and all of their children were as well, and their grandchildren and so on, until they broke faith and bedded mortals.<br /> <br /> Those who bore a Genesis Engine, however, were always a cut above the rest, having certain attributes their fellows did not, earning them the title of Dragonlords. Individually, a Dragonlord was no more powerful than other Dragonblooded, but with other Dragonblooded, she quite specifically demonstrated what she was. By instinct, Dragonblooded will follow a Dragonlord and Dragonlords treated their followers as descendants. The older and more powerful a Dragonlord became, the more Dragonblooded followers he accrued.<br /> <br /> During the Primordial War, the Elemental Dragons would grant the Engines to mortals without a drop of dragon's blood when a previous Dragonlord died, better allowing the Dragonblooded to spread and overwhelm the soon-to-be Fallen. Afterwards, when their attention turned to the upkeep of Creation, they gave the Engines to the Incarnae to hand out as they willed. The Incarnae lacked the power to give the Engines to one who did not already have the blood of dragons but they gave them more freely with having them more numerous, each Incarnae applying their own particular prejudice to who should get them.<br /> <br /> If the Dragonblooded were the footsoldiers of the Exalted Host, the Dragonlords were its sergeants, directly leading their brothers into battle. Terrestrial Exalts who stand among Celestials and can be called equals are often this sort, calling upon the power of a growing host of others to face the Exalted Of Heaven. One Dragonlord attracted the attention of the Incarnae when she held the whole of Creation in the palm of her hand and built an empire from the power granted to her there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}